!! Tags

| Tag | Purpose |
|`$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/note` | identifies a knowledge note for `knowledge.notes()` and friends |
|`$:/tags/rimir/appify/app` | (on `apps/knowledge`) registers the app with appify |
|`$:/tags/rimir/appify/view` | (on `views/*`, `apps/knowledge-topbar`, `apps/knowledge-sidebar`) marks an appify view tiddler |
|`$:/tags/NamespaceMount` | (on `config/starter-mount`) registers the `kn` mount |
|`$:/tags/Stylesheet` | (on `styles`) makes the CSS shadow active |
|`$:/tags/test-spec` | (on `test/test-*.js`) discovered by the Jasmine runner |

!! Channels

| Channel | Domain |
|`section`| `home` \| `browse` \| `note` \| `write` \| `search` |
|`topic` | first segment after `knowledge/` (or empty) |
|`note` | full title of the focused note (or empty) |

!! State tiddlers

| Title | Use |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/open` | "yes" while quick-capture modal is visible |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/title` | bound to the modal's title input |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/body` | bound to the modal's body textarea |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/type` | bound to the modal's type select |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/source/<field>` | per-field state for the source capture form (`caption`, `author`, `medium`, `url`, `published`, `published-mode`, `consume-status`, `consume-date`) |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/last-saved` | title of the most recently captured note |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/source-edit/<noteTitle>` | name of the source field currently being inline-edited (or blank) |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/source-yt-size/<noteTitle>` | `small` (default) / `medium` / `large` — chosen YouTube player size |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/search-query` | live search input |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/browse/tier` | currently active tier chip in Browse |

!! Config tiddlers

| Title | Default |
|`$:/config/rimir/knowledge-app/stub-threshold` | `200` |
|`$:/config/rimir/knowledge-app/capture-prefix` | `knowledge/inbox/` |
|`$:/config/rimir/namespace/walk-up` | `yes` (this plugin overrides the namespace default) |
|`$:/config/rimir/namespace/aliases` | `yes` |
|`$:/config/rimir/namespace/pseudo-expansion` | `yes` |

!! Filter operators (defined here)

* `[<title>knowledge-has-broken-ref[]]` — input title if its body contains at least one unresolved `[[…]]`, else nothing.

!! Filter functions

* `\function knowledge.notes()` — all knowledge notes
* `\function knowledge.orphans()` — zero backlinks
* `\function knowledge.dead-ends()` — zero forward links
* `\function knowledge.stubs()` — body length below threshold
* `\function knowledge.broken()` — at least one unresolved ref

!! Source helper functions

Defined in `forms/source-helpers.tid`, imported by `forms/capture-source` and `forms/render-source` via `\import`.

* `\function knowledge.yt-id(url)` — extracts the 11-char YouTube video ID from `watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` or `/embed/` URL forms; empty when the URL doesn't parse.
* `\function knowledge.medium-icon(medium)` — emoji per medium type (article 📰, book 📕, youtube 📺, podcast 🎙, blog ✍, fallback 🔗).
* `\function knowledge.consume-icon(status)` — emoji per consume status (created ✏, partial ⏳, consumed ✅, reconsumed 🔁, fallback •).

!! Type-specific form tiddlers

| Title | Use |
|`forms/capture-<type>` | extra modal fields for `<type>`. Transcluded by `procedures/quick-capture-modal` when the type select matches |
|`forms/render-<type>` | structured display for `<type>`. Transcluded by `views/note` above the body when the note's `kn.type` matches |
|`forms/<type>-helpers` | shared `\function`s for the type's two halves (imported via `\import`) |

!! Pseudo modules

* `_index` — resolves to `index` or `README` under the prefix.

